&lt;p&gt;Here, &lt;strong&gt;impact in your role matters more than title&lt;/strong&gt; and trust is built on results. We say, impact over activity. We seek innovators who actively use AI to amplify their impact and who thrive in an environment where we leverage intelligent systems to stay ahead of evolving threats. We believe in transparency and value &lt;strong&gt;constructive, honest debate&lt;/strong&gt;—we’re focused on getting to the best ideas, faster. We build high-performing teams that can make an impact quickly and with high quality. To do this, we are building a culture of execution centered on &lt;strong&gt;customer obsession&lt;/strong&gt;, collaboration, ownership, and accountability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value high-impact, high-accountability with a sense of urgency where you’re enabled to do your best work and embrace your potential. If you’re driven by purpose, thrive on solving complex challenges, and want to be part of the team that’s helping to secure the AI age, we invite you to bring your talents to Zscaler and help shape the future of cybersecurity.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Staff Technical Program Manager to join our Engineering Operations team. This is a hybrid role based in the San Jose, CA office 3 days a week, reporting to the Sr Director, Engineering Operations. The TPM will join Zscaler’s central Technical Program Management team and partner directly with the Engineering Lead at Zscaler. This role is responsible for establishing a clear intake and commitment process, leading execution and delivery reviews to ensure programs stay on track, and driving release readiness criteria to meet Zscaler’s quality bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do (Role Expectations)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive program planning and definition to ensure the successful adoption of SDLC efforts within your functional area&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead weekly execution reviews covering product initiatives, production incidents, service health, OKRs, and technical deep-dives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee release content planning for current releases, active development, and future roadmaps&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and present program reviews using JIRA structures to eliminate manual tracking and ensure clear communication across the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement opportunities to improve existing development processes and toolsets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are (Success Profile)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You act like an owner by fueling your bias for action with a passion for the mission, operating with integrity, and navigating between high-level strategy and hands-on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a high-trust collaborator who is ambitious for the team, embracing a challenge culture through candid feedback delivered with clarity and respect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are customer-obsessed, building deep empathy for internal and external customers to anchor decisions in solving real-world problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You champion simplicity by distilling complex technical concepts into clear, actionable plans and bringing precise focus to every interaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You think at scale by connecting day-to-day work to the global company mission and building processes that support a high-growth organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking for (Minimum Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in Engineering or Technical Program Management, with at least 2 years specifically in a TPM role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Undergraduate degree in Engineering, Business, or a related domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven bias for action with the ability to take smart risks and demonstrate incremental progress&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success in stakeholder management with the ability to communicate effectively across all levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical proficiency in JIRA, including JIRA dashboards, JIRA Structure, and advanced tracking methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will Make You Stand Out (Preferred Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior hands-on engineering experience, specifically dealing with low-level networking (protocols, network configuration, routing, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of the networking industry with the technical depth to identify risks and translate complex architectural challenges into actionable plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
