&lt;li&gt;You are a pragmatic builder. You are obsessed with creating, iterating, and shipping. You aren&#39;t afraid to roll up your sleeves and build the first version yourself, balancing the drive for technical excellence with the need to deliver value to users quickly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You champion simplicity. You are skilled at distilling complex problems, user needs, and technical concepts into clear, simple, and actionable plans. You are a precise communicator who brings clarity and focus to every interaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking for (Minimum Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;US Citizenship and an active Top Secret Security Clearance, with the ability to work from a SCIF.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of Site Reliability Engineering experience in both Operations and Engineering environments, including Python coding and container-based architectures such as AWS ECS or Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current Active Duty United States military member or a member of the United States Guard/Reserve component on active duty orders for at least the last 180 days with 180 days or fewer remaining prior to discharge.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unit commander approval.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MOU approved and submitted before start.&lt;/li&gt;
