&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Staff Technical Program Manager (Federal Authorizations) to join our team. Although the role can be remote within the US, there is a preference for someone to work in a hybrid environment from the San Jose, CA office.&amp;nbsp; This role reports to the Director of Technology Compliance within the Exposure Management and Security Operations department.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zscaler is seeking an experienced Staff Technical Program Manager (Federal Authorizations) to own and drive the end-to-end federal authorization roadmap across FedRAMP and DoD programs. This role operates with a product-manager mindset, defining the authorization strategy and roadmap, establishing clear priorities and success criteria, and driving cross-functional execution from onboarding through authorization and ongoing sustainment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do (Role Expectations)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full federal authorization roadmap across impact levels (e.g., FedRAMP Moderate, High, IL2/4/5/6) and maintain authorization packages ensuring completeness, accuracy, and auditability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate end-to-end assessments and manage artifact submission timelines, review cycles, and official authorization communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure timely and accurate delivery of Continuous Monitoring (ConMon) reporting while partnering with Compliance Engineering to automate evidence collection workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary interface with authorizing officials and government stakeholders to ensure clear communication, predictable timelines, and professional stakeholder management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish program operating mechanisms and governance, providing clear reporting to leadership while ensuring cross-functional accountability across Product, Engineering, and GTM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are (Success Profile)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You thrive in ambiguity. You&#39;re comfortable building the path as you walk it. You thrive in a dynamic environment, seeing ambiguity not as a hindrance, but as the raw material to build something meaningful.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You act like an owner. Your passion for the mission fuels your bias for action. You operate with integrity because you genuinely care about the outcome. True ownership involves leveraging dynamic range: the ability to navigate seamlessly between high-level strategy and hands-on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a problem-solver. You love running towards the challenges because you are laser-focused on finding the solution, knowing that solving the hard problems delivers the biggest impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a high-trust collaborator. You are ambitious for the team, not just yourself. You embrace our challenge culture by giving and receiving ongoing feedback—knowing that candor delivered with clarity and respect is the truest form of teamwork and the fastest way to earn trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a learner. You have a true growth mindset and are obsessed with your own development, actively seeking feedback to become a better partner and a stronger teammate. You love what you do and you do it with purpose.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking for (Minimum Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Information Systems, or a related field (or equivalent practical experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in Technical Program Management or Security/Compliance Program Management driving complex cross-functional initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience managing federal authorization or compliance programs (e.g., FedRAMP, DoD, NIST-based assessments) and associated evidence workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ability to operate as a “product-like” owner with expertise in roadmap definition, prioritization, and outcome-based delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience coordinating assessments and driving closure across technical and non-technical stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Will Make You Stand Out (Preferred Qualifications)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience owning or coordinating FedRAMP/DoD ATO packages, ConMon submissions, and interactions with authorizing officials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with NIST control frameworks and experience partnering with engineering teams on compliance evidence automation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional certifications such as PMP, PgMP, or CISM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
